#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""codexpool: operate the pool of ChatGPT seats behind the Codex desktop app.

The request path is the Codex app (or CLI) -> CLIProxyAPI (127.0.0.1:8319 by default) -> chatgpt.com,
with one OAuth login per seat in ~/.codexpool/auth. CLIProxyAPI is built from its upstream release
source plus one file, build/codexpool_gate.go, which refuses browser and non-loopback requests. This
tool never sits in the request path: it reads and nudges the pool through the management API (key in
the macOS Keychain) and never prints tokens. `codexpool guard` runs every minute from launchd.

Optional lanes (~/.codexpool/lanes.json, `codexpool lane`) let the Codex main agent spawn third-party models as
native subagents. They touch only lane model requests: CLIProxyAPI payload rules, and for providers the pool does
not speak natively, lanes/bridge.py, an upstream that sits behind the pool. Seat traffic never reaches either.

Per-machine settings (launchd labels, port, interpreters, the codex binary) live in
~/.codexpool/settings.json (CODEXPOOL_SETTINGS points elsewhere). `codexpool install` sets everything
up and is safe to re-run; `codexpool uninstall` undoes it.
"""
